      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The legs of the right triangle are $\\log_4 27$ and $\\log_2 9.$\nUsing the change of base formula, we can rewrite these as $\\frac{\\log 27}{\\log 4}$ and $\\frac{\\log 9}{\\log 2}.$\nTherefore, the length of the hypotenuse is $\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\log 27}{\\log 4}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\log 9}{\\log 2}\\right)^2}.$\nWe can simplify this expression using the property $\\log_b a = \\frac{\\log_c a}{\\log_c b}.$\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\log 27}{\\log 4}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\log 9}{\\log 2}\\right)^2} &= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\log 27}{\\log 4}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\log 3^2}{\\log 2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\log 27}{\\log 4}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{2\\log 3}{\\log 2}\\right)^2}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3\\log 3}{2\\log 2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{2\\log 3}{\\log 2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3\\log 3}{2\\log 2}\\right)^2+4\\left(\\frac{2\\log 3}{\\log 2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3\\log 3}{2\\log 2}\\right)^2\\left(\\frac{9+16}{9}\\right)} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3\\log 3}{2\\log 2}\\right)^2\\left(\\frac{25}{9}\\right)} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3\\log 3}{2\\log 2}\\right)^2\\left(\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)^2\\right)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{3}\\log 3 \\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\log 2 \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{2}\\log 3 \\cdot \\log 2 \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{2}\\log 6 \\\\\n&= \\log_6 6^5 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{5}.\n\\end{align*}\nThe answer is: 5",
